{
  "id": "plural",
  "name": "Plurals of nouns and adjectives",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "it-IT",
  "subtitle": "Italian changes the last vowel: -o and -e become -i, -a becomes -e (il libro → i libri, la chiave → le chiavi, la casa → le case). The article and the adjective change too: le case bianche.",
  "briefMarks": ["-o → -i", "-e → -i", "-a → -e", "i", "gli", "le"],
  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "i / gli / le", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun: -i / -e", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "adjective: -i / -e", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "libr<span class=\"vp-verb\">o</span> → libr<span class=\"vp-verb\">i</span> · chiav<span class=\"vp-verb\">e</span> → chiav<span class=\"vp-verb\">i</span> · cas<span class=\"vp-verb\">a</span> → cas<span class=\"vp-verb\">e</span> · il treno nuovo → <span class=\"vp-prep\">i</span> tren<span class=\"vp-verb\">i</span> nuov<span class=\"vp-verb\">i</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>-o → -i</strong>: <em>il libro → i libri, il treno → i treni, il documento → i documenti</em>.",
        "tag": "-o → -i"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>-a → -e</strong> for feminine nouns: <em>la casa → le case, la strada → le strade</em>. Masculine nouns in -a take <strong>-i</strong>: <em>il problema → i problemi</em>.",
        "tag": "-a → -e"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>-e → -i</strong>, for masculine and feminine nouns: <em>il giornale → i giornali, la chiave → le chiavi, la lezione → le lezioni</em>.",
        "tag": "-e → -i"
      },
      {
        "html": "Some nouns <strong>do not change</strong>. Only the article shows the plural: words with an accent on the last vowel (<em>la città → le città, il caffè → i caffè</em>), words that end in a consonant (<em>il bar → i bar, il film → i film</em>) and short words (<em>la foto → le foto, la moto → le moto</em>).",
        "tag": "No change"
      },
      {
        "html": "Keep the hard sound: <strong>-ca → -che</strong>, <strong>-ga → -ghe</strong>: <em>l'amica → le amiche, la banca → le banche</em>. Words in <strong>-co, -go</strong> often take <strong>-chi, -ghi</strong> (<em>il parco → i parchi, l'albergo → gli alberghi</em>), but some take <strong>-ci</strong>: <em>l'amico → gli amici, il medico → i medici</em>.",
        "tag": "c and g"
      },
      {
        "html": "A few plurals are irregular: <em>l'uomo → gli uomini, la mano → le mani, l'uovo → le uova</em> (<em>uova</em> is feminine: <em>le uova</em>).",
        "tag": "Irregular"
      },
      {
        "html": "Everything around the noun changes too: <em><strong>la</strong> casa bianc<strong>a</strong> → <strong>le</strong> case bianch<strong>e</strong></em>. A group of men and women takes the masculine: <em>i vicini</em> can be men and women.",
        "tag": "Agreement"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>le amice</em> → ✓ <em>le amiche</em>. ✗ <em>le citte</em> → ✓ <em>le città</em>. ✗ <em>i uomini</em> → ✓ <em>gli uomini</em>. ✗ <em>i case</em> → ✓ <em>le case</em>. The plural articles: <a href=\"/articles\">Articles</a>. More on adjectives: <a href=\"/adjective-agreement\">Adjectives: agreement and position</a>.",
    "reference": {
